module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionOfSurfaces.RationalSingularities.ExceptionalIdealPowers
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Immersion.FibreIdealSheaf

/-!
# The ideal sheaf of the special fibre is `𝔪 𝒪_X`, and is generated by global sections

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] — a two-dimensional local normal Nagata domain `A` defining a
rational singularity and a modification `f : X ⟶ Spec(A)` with normal source — the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0B4Y] opens by identifying the ideal sheaf `𝓘` of the special fibre `E = X_s` with
the extension `𝔪 𝒪_X` of the maximal ideal, and then observes that `𝔪 𝒪_X` is generated by
global sections, namely by the images of the elements of `𝔪`.

Both steps are proved here, by specialising the general statements of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Immersion.FibreIdealSheaf`: the identification is the
ideal assertion of [Stacks, Tag 01JU] part (1) over the affine base `Spec(A)`, and the global
generation is `Stacks.Divisors.nonempty_generatingSections_ofIdealTop`.

Nothing in the rational singularity situation is used: the two statements hold for an arbitrary
morphism to the spectrum of a local ring.  They are recorded at
`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation` because that is where `𝓘` is named.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.exceptionalIdeal_eq_baseIdealSheaf`:
  **`𝓘 = 𝔪 𝒪_X`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.nonempty_generatingSections_exceptionalIdeal`:
  **`𝓘` is generated by global sections.**  This is the global generation on which the
  first-cohomology conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0B4Y],
  `RationalSingularitySituation.isZero_firstCohomology_exceptionalIdealPow_unconditional` in the
  namespace `AlgebraicGeometry`, rests.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.exceptionalIdealPowGeneratingSections'`:
  generating global sections of every power `𝓘ⁿ`, with no hypothesis.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01JU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01JU)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation

variable (S : RationalSingularitySituation.{u})

/-- **`𝓘 = 𝔪 𝒪_X`.**  The ideal sheaf of the special fibre `E = X_s` is the extension to `X` of
the maximal ideal of `A`.  This is the ideal assertion of [Stacks, Tag 01JU] part (1) at the
affine base `Spec(A)`. -/
theorem exceptionalIdeal_eq_baseIdealSheaf :
    S.exceptionalIdeal =
      Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf S.A S.maximalIdeal S.f :=
  Stacks.IdealSheaf.ker_fiberι_closedPoint S.f

/-- **The ideal sheaf of the special fibre is generated by global sections.**  It is `𝔪 𝒪_X` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.exceptionalIdeal_eq_baseIdealSheaf`, hence
generated by the global functions it contains. -/
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_exceptionalIdeal :
    Nonempty (Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafOfModules S.exceptionalIdeal).GeneratingSections :=
  Stacks.IdealSheaf.nonempty_generatingSections_ker_fiberι_closedPoint S.f

/-- **Generating global sections of every power of the ideal sheaf of the special fibre**, with
no hypothesis: the products of the images of the generators of `𝔪` do the job. -/
noncomputable def exceptionalIdealPowGeneratingSections' (n : ℕ) :
    (S.exceptionalIdealPow n).GeneratingSections :=
  S.exceptionalIdealPowGeneratingSections
    S.nonempty_generatingSections_exceptionalIdeal.some n

end AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation

end
